markoto bundles and depends on third-party open-source software, each under
its own license, including (non-exhaustively): Nuxt, Vue, CodeMirror, Y.js,
Hocuspocus, y-postgresql, markdown-it and the @mdit plugin family, KaTeX,
Mermaid, highlight.js, paged.js, DOMPurify, Drizzle ORM, node-postgres,
ioredis, Stripe SDK, LiteLLM, and Markitdown. The full dependency set and
license metadata are recorded in package.json / bun.lock of each workspace
(root, sync-server/, renderer/, markitdown-server/).

renderer/seccomp.json is derived from the Moby project's default seccomp profile
(https://github.com/moby/profiles, seccomp/default.json), licensed under the
Apache License 2.0, with one added rule for Chromium's sandbox.

Bundled fonts (committed under fonts/, served from this origin; each directory
carries its licence and manifest):
- TeX Gyre Termes and TeX Gyre Heros (fonts/tex-gyre-*), GUST e-foundry,
  GUST Font License (LPPL 1.3c based), http://www.gust.org.pl/projects/e-foundry/tex-gyre
- Latin Modern Roman and Latin Modern Mono (fonts/latin-modern-*), GUST
  e-foundry, GUST Font License, http://www.gust.org.pl/projects/e-foundry/latin-modern
- Greek companion files in fonts/latin-modern-*/cmu-greek-*, subset of CM
  Unicode 0.7.0 by Andrey V. Panov, SIL Open Font License 1.1,
  https://ctan.org/pkg/cm-unicode (renamed "markoto Greek Serif" per the
  Reserved Font Name clause)

Web fonts installed from npm, devDependencies, SIL Open Font License 1.1: the
@fontsource and @fontsource-variable packages listed in shared/utils/theme/themeFonts.ts
(https://fontsource.org), each repackaging the upstream font under its own OFL
copyright; the licence text ships in each package and is copied next to the
served files under /vendor/.

Browser libraries served from this origin under /vendor/ (copied from the pinned
npm packages at build time, versions in shared/utils/vendor/*Assets.ts):
- paged.js, MIT, https://github.com/pagedjs/pagedjs
- KaTeX (stylesheet and fonts), MIT, https://github.com/KaTeX/KaTeX
- Mermaid, MIT, https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid
- highlight.js (theme stylesheets), BSD-3-Clause, https://github.com/highlightjs/highlight.js

Avatars: the "Moods" style from @dicebear/styles by DiceBear, CC0 1.0,
